\details{
\subsection{Risk and Expected Loss}{

For each ensemble realization at each zone location, classify as:
\itemize{
\item \strong{"Too low"}: X < threshold → incurs cost_under
\item \strong{"In range"}: X >= threshold → incurs zero cost
\item \strong{"Too high"}: X > threshold → incurs cost_over (if specified)
}

Expected loss = E\link{cost | zone, X}:

$$EL = P(X < \theta) \times cost_{under} + P(X > \theta) \times cost_{over}$$

\strong{Asymmetry motivates per-zone decisions}: A farmer might accept higher clay in lowlands
(cost_over small, landscape adapted) but penalize clay in uplands (cost_over large, limits drainage).
}

